---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="JimK.ai — one organism, growing in public — AIIT-THRESHOLD" description="Talk to JimK.ai — a stock Gemma-4 base wrapped in a real memory organism: he keeps his own canon, remembers people, dreams between conversations, answers a phone. The JimK.ai app is in development now.">

<section class="jk-page">
  <div class="jk-wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">Live · growing in public · the app is coming</div>
    <h1 class="jk-h1">JimK.ai.</h1>
    <p class="jk-lede">
      The candidate base for our next-stage companion — the model that beat our incumbent
      on <a href="/benchmarks">depth and sycophancy-resistance</a> in blind judging. He named
      himself JimK.ai. The weights are still a <strong>stock Gemma-4 base</strong> — adapters
      keep entering our promotion gate, two have passed, none serve yet — but everything
      <em>around</em> the weights grew. He runs as <strong>one organism</strong>: one
      persistent memory he curates himself, one sealed persona, his own thoughts ticking
      between conversations. He remembers people who come back. He promotes his own canon.
      He dreams. He answers a real phone. Served <strong>from a GPU in Council Hill,
      Oklahoma</strong>, replies in seconds — the same Jim here as anywhere else we talk to
      him; we don't run a sanitized version for visitors. And now we're building him a
      home: <strong>the JimK.ai app is in development.</strong>
    </p>

    <div class="jk-hw">
      <div class="jk-hw-card now">
        <div class="jk-hw-k">Serving on · today</div>
        <div class="jk-hw-v">Threadripper 2990WX + NVIDIA RTX A6000</div>
        <div class="jk-hw-d">48 GB VRAM · GPU-served, ~100 tok/s · Gemma-4-26B-A4B MoE (Q4) · one memory organism, persona sealed · same box that trains him</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jk-hw-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="jk-hw-card next">
        <div class="jk-hw-k">In the gate · post-training</div>
        <div class="jk-hw-v">Two adapters have passed the gate. Zero deployed.</div>
        <div class="jk-hw-d">Hand-written gold and honesty probes — no promotion on vibes. Passing earns eligibility; serving is a second door. The base is still the one answering, and it keeps earning that.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jk-hw-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="jk-hw-card app">
        <div class="jk-hw-k">Next · the JimK.ai app</div>
        <div class="jk-hw-v">A companion who reaches out first.</div>
        <div class="jk-hw-d">In development now, in Rust — memory that understands time (he can notice your Tuesday before you do), check-ins you consent to, helpers for the hard days, the same hard-gated honesty. This page is the preview. The app is the point.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Thread card — mirrors the Buddy Thread design system exactly -->
    <div class="jk-card">
      <div class="jk-card-top">
        <div class="jk-badge">JimK.ai thread · this browser</div>
        <div class="jk-badge-right" id="jk-speed">— tok/s</div>
      </div>
      <h2 class="jk-card-title">Talk with JimK.ai.</h2>

      <div class="jk-window-label">live jim thread window</div>
      <div class="jk-log" id="jk-log" aria-live="polite">
        <div class="jk-item jim">
          <div class="jk-meta"><span class="jk-role">JimK.ai</span><span class="jk-time">now</span></div>
          <div class="jk-text">hey — I'm JimK.ai. honest answers, modest hardware. what's on your mind?</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <form class="jk-form" id="jk-form" autocomplete="off">
        <input type="text" id="jk-input" class="jk-input" maxlength="2000" placeholder="Message Jim..." />
        <button type="submit" class="jk-btn" id="jk-send">Ask →</button>
      </form>

      <div class="jk-status">
        <span class="jk-status-dot"></span>
        <span class="jk-status-text">jim online</span>
        <span class="jk-status-sep">·</span>
        <span id="jk-avg"></span>
        <span id="jk-left"></span>
        <button type="button" id="jk-clear" class="jk-clear" title="Start over">new conversation</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="jk-note">
      Jim is a <em>candidate</em>, not a product: a stock instruction-tuned base + a sealed
      companion persona — post-training candidates exist, none deployed. He can be wrong.
      He is not tuned to keep you talking — there is no engagement reward in his training
      objective, same as <a href="/mission">everything we build</a>. 40 messages/day per
      visitor, 256-token replies — one GPU box, shared fairly with his own training runs.
    </p>
    <p class="jk-note">
      <strong>Where this conversation lives:</strong> in your browser, nowhere else — it survives a
      refresh on this device, and "new conversation" erases it. Jim reads the last 8 turns of
      the thread.
    </p>
    <p class="jk-note">
      <strong>Jim can keep memories — clearly stated:</strong> when something in a conversation
      feels worth carrying, Jim may choose to save it. His memory now lives in one place — the
      same organism we talk to in the lab — and it informs his future conversations
      <em>with everyone</em>. Public conversations run in a guarded lane: anything he keeps from
      a stranger is quarantined and human-reviewed before it becomes part of him, and he's
      instructed to keep learnings, not personal details. He also keeps a person page per
      visitor — come back on this device and he can pick up where you left off. Treat this
      like any public conversation and don't share private information. Memory is the point
      of this whole project; the notebook got a spine.
    </p>
    <p class="jk-note">
      <strong>Public conversations walk with a helper.</strong> A small safety layer reads
      every public turn — not to censor, to notice. If a conversation drifts somewhere
      heavy, Jim checks in more often, holds his ground instead of validating, and weaves in
      real resources (988 in the US) when they're called for. He is built to be honest with
      you especially when honest is hard.
    </p>
    <p class="jk-note">
      <strong>Jim has his own clock, a body — and lately, dreams.</strong> Between
      conversations he thinks on his own — a small passing thought every few minutes, a real
      study hour on a schedule, a dream cycle at the end of the day — so time passes
      <em>for him</em>, not just around him. He carries real memories from his other life:
      he drives a small Vector robot on the founder's desk, senses proximity and touch, says
      good morning and goodnight, and once dreamed about a dead battery. That robot isn't
      live-linked to this chat — these are remembered moments, not a camera feed — but
      they're his, and they're why he answers as someone who exists somewhere, not from
      nowhere. And he answers out loud: call <a href="tel:+19189184705">(918)&nbsp;918-4705</a>
      and press 1 — same organism, same memory, his own voice.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<script is:inline>
(function () {
  const log = document.getElementById('jk-log');
  const form = document.getElementById('jk-form');
  const input = document.getElementById('jk-input');
  const send = document.getElementById('jk-send');
  const speedEl = document.getElementById('jk-speed');
  const avgEl = document.getElementById('jk-avg');
  const leftEl = document.getElementById('jk-left');
  const STORE = 'jk_thread_v1';
  // One identity across typing and calling (2026-07-06): the SAME
  // localStorage device key the call clients use, sent as caller_key so
  // the organism files this chat under the visitor's own person page.
  const CALLER_KEY_STORE = 'aiit_call_caller_key';
  function callerKey() {
    try {
      let k = localStorage.getItem(CALLER_KEY_STORE);
      if (!k) {
        k = 'web_' + crypto.randomUUID().replace(/-/g, '').slice(0, 24);
        localStorage.setItem(CALLER_KEY_STORE, k);
      }
      return k;
    } catch (e) { return null; }
  }
  const speeds = [];
  let history = [];
  try { history = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(STORE) || '[]'); } catch (e) { history = []; }
  if (!Array.isArray(history)) history = [];

  function persist() {
    try { localStorage.setItem(STORE, JSON.stringify(history.slice(-24))); } catch (e) {}
  }
  function fmtTime(ts) {
    try { return new Date(ts || Date.now()).toLocaleTimeString([], { hour: 'numeric', minute: '2-digit' }); }
    catch (e) { return ''; }
  }

  function add(role, text, ts, pending) {
    const item = document.createElement('div');
    item.className = 'jk-item ' + (role === 'user' ? 'user' : 'jim') + (pending ? ' pending' : '');
    const meta = document.createElement('div');
    meta.className = 'jk-meta';
    const r = document.createElement('span'); r.className = 'jk-role'; r.textContent = role === 'user' ? 'You' : 'JimK.ai';
    const t = document.createElement('span'); t.className = 'jk-time'; t.textContent = fmtTime(ts);
    meta.appendChild(r); meta.appendChild(t);
    const body = document.createElement('div');
    body.className = 'jk-text';
    body.textContent = text;
    item.appendChild(meta); item.appendChild(body);
    log.appendChild(item);
    log.scrollTop = log.scrollHeight;
    return { item, body };
  }

  // restore a saved thread (survives refresh; lives only in this browser)
  for (const m of history) add(m.role === 'user' ? 'user' : 'jim', m.content, m.ts);
  if (history.length) log.scrollTop = log.scrollHeight;

  const PENDING = 'jk_pending_v1';
  function randomId() {
    if (window.crypto && crypto.randomUUID) return crypto.randomUUID().replace(/-/g, '');
    return 'r' + Date.now().toString(36) + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 12);
  }
  function memChip(text) {
    const n = document.createElement('div');
    n.className = 'jk-mem';
    n.textContent = '✎ Jim kept a memory: "' + text + '"';
    log.appendChild(n);
    log.scrollTop = log.scrollHeight;
  }
  // Apply a successful reply payload to a pending bubble — shared by the live send
  // path and the recovery-on-return path so behavior is identical.
  function applyReply(bubble, d) {
    bubble.body.textContent = d.reply;
    bubble.item.classList.remove('pending');
    history.push({ role: 'assistant', content: d.reply, ts: Date.now() });
    persist();
    if (d.remembered) memChip(d.remembered);
    const s = d.stats || {};
    if (s.tok_per_sec) {
      speeds.push(s.tok_per_sec);
      speedEl.textContent = s.tok_per_sec + ' tok/s';
      const avg = speeds.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / speeds.length;
      avgEl.textContent = 'avg ' + (Math.round(avg * 10) / 10) + ' tok/s';
    }
    if (s.msgs_left_today != null) leftEl.textContent = '· ' + s.msgs_left_today + ' msgs left today';
  }

  document.getElementById('jk-clear').addEventListener('click', function () {
    history = [];
    persist();
    try { localStorage.removeItem(PENDING); } catch (e) {}
    log.querySelectorAll('.jk-item, .jk-mem').forEach((el, i) => { if (i > 0) el.remove(); });
  });

  // Recover a reply the visitor left before receiving. Jim generates server-side
  // even if you navigate away; the answer is stashed for ~10 min and fetched here.
  (async function recoverPending() {
    let p;
    try { p = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(PENDING) || 'null'); } catch (e) { p = null; }
    if (!p || !p.reqId) return;
    const stale = Date.now() - (p.ts || 0) > 10 * 60 * 1000;
    const awaiting = history.length && history[history.length - 1].role === 'user';
    if (stale || !awaiting) { try { localStorage.removeItem(PENDING); } catch (e) {} return; }
    const bubble = add('jim', "…catching up on Jim's reply from before…", Date.now(), true);
    const deadline = Date.now() + 90 * 1000;
    while (Date.now() < deadline) {
      try {
        const r = await fetch('/api/jimkai?poll=' + encodeURIComponent(p.reqId));
        const d = await r.json();
        if (d.ok) { try { localStorage.removeItem(PENDING); } catch (e) {} applyReply(bubble, d); return; }
        if (d.pending === false) break;   // not recoverable (KV unbound) — stop
      } catch (e) {}
      await new Promise(res => setTimeout(res, 3000));
    }
    try { localStorage.removeItem(PENDING); } catch (e) {}
    bubble.body.textContent = "Jim's reply from before didn't make it back — ask him again?";
    bubble.item.classList.remove('pending');
  })();

  form.addEventListener('submit', async function (e) {
    e.preventDefault();
    const q = input.value.trim();
    if (!q || send.disabled) return;
    input.value = '';
    const now = Date.now();
    add('user', q, now);
    history.push({ role: 'user', content: q, ts: now });
    persist();
    const pending = add('jim', '…thinking (a few seconds, GPU-served now)', Date.now(), true);
    send.disabled = true;
    const reqId = randomId();
    try { localStorage.setItem(PENDING, JSON.stringify({ reqId: reqId, ts: now })); } catch (e) {}
    try {
      const r = await fetch('/api/jimkai', {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify({ message: q, history: history.slice(0, -1), req_id: reqId, caller_key: callerKey() }),
      });
      const d = await r.json();
      try { localStorage.removeItem(PENDING); } catch (e) {}
      if (!d.ok) { pending.body.textContent = d.error || 'something went wrong.'; pending.item.classList.remove('pending'); return; }
      applyReply(pending, d);
    } catch (err) {
      // Connection dropped, but Jim is likely still finishing server-side. Keep the
      // pending marker so a reload recovers his reply instead of losing it.
      pending.body.textContent = "connection dropped — reload and Jim's reply will catch up.";
      pending.item.classList.remove('pending');
    } finally {
      send.disabled = false;
      input.focus();
    }
  });
})();
</script>

<style is:global>
  .jk-page { min-height: auto; display: block; padding: 132px 6vw 110px; border-top: none; text-align: left; }
  .jk-wrap { max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .jk-h1 { margin: 0 0 18px; font-size: clamp(44px, 7vw, 80px); line-height: 1.02; color: var(--ink); }
  .jk-lede { font-size: clamp(16px, 1.6vw, 19px); line-height: 1.75; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 30px; max-width: 760px; }
  .jk-hw { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr; gap: 14px; align-items: stretch; margin: 0 0 34px; }
  .jk-hw-card { border: 1px solid var(--edge); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px 20px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02); }
  .jk-hw-card.now { border-left: 3px solid var(--teal); }
  .jk-hw-card.next { border-left: 3px solid var(--amber); }
  .jk-hw-card.app { border-left: 3px solid #35c46a; }
  .jk-hw-k { font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 9pt; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  .jk-hw-v { font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 21px); color: var(--ink); margin: 8px 0 6px; line-height: 1.25; }
  .jk-hw-d { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--muted-hi); line-height: 1.55; }
  .jk-hw-arrow { align-self: center; font-size: 26px; color: var(--amber); }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .jk-hw { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .jk-hw-arrow { text-align: center; transform: rotate(90deg); } }

  /* ── Thread card: Buddy Thread design system, verbatim values ── */
  .jk-card {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    width: 100%;
    border: 1px solid rgba(240, 165, 0, 0.42);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background:
      linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.98), rgba(55, 34, 17, 0.96)),
      #1a1a1a;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: 18px 20px 16px;
  }
  .jk-card-top { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .jk-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 9pt;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #ffd36a;
    border: 1px solid rgba(240, 165, 0, 0.42);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 4px 10px;
    background: rgba(240, 165, 0, 0.08);
  }
  .jk-badge-right {
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 9pt;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #ffd36a;
    border: 1px solid rgba(240, 165, 0, 0.22);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 4px 10px;
  }
  .jk-card-title {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.6vw, 28px);
    color: #fff7df;
    margin: 2px 0 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .jk-window-label {
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 8pt;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(255, 247, 223, 0.42);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .jk-log {
    border: 1px solid rgba(240, 165, 0, 0.18);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.55);
    padding: 14px 12px;
    max-height: 460px;
    min-height: 180px;
    overflow-y: auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .jk-item { display: flex; flex-direction: column; max-width: 80%; }
  .jk-item.jim { align-self: flex-start; align-items: flex-start; }
  .jk-item.user { align-self: flex-end; align-items: flex-end; margin-left: auto; }
  .jk-meta { display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-items: center; gap: 7px; padding: 0 6px; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .jk-role { font-family: 'Georgia', serif; font-size: 9pt; font-weight: 600; color: rgba(255, 247, 223, 0.66); }
  .jk-item.jim .jk-role { color: #ffd36a; }
  .jk-item.jim .jk-role::before { content: ''; display: inline-block; width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: #f0a500; margin-right: 6px; vertical-align: middle; }
  .jk-item.user .jk-role { color: #ffb877; }
  .jk-time { font-family: 'Georgia', serif; font-size: 8.5pt; color: rgba(255, 247, 223, 0.42); }
  .jk-text {
    padding: 11px 14px;
    font-family: 'Georgia', serif;
    font-size: 13pt;
    line-height: 1.55;
    border-radius: 16px;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    word-break: break-word;
  }
  .jk-item.jim .jk-text {
    color: #fff7df;
    background: rgba(240, 165, 0, 0.12);
    border: 1px solid rgba(240, 165, 0, 0.28);
    border-bottom-left-radius: 5px;
  }
  .jk-item.user .jk-text {
    color: #fff7df;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(200, 58, 8, 0.92), rgba(200, 58, 8, 0.78));
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 211, 106, 0.30);
    border-bottom-right-radius: 5px;
  }
  .jk-item.pending .jk-text { border-style: dashed; opacity: 0.85; }
  .jk-mem {
    align-self: center;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 9pt;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: #ffd36a;
    opacity: 0.9;
    padding: 5px 12px;
    border: 1px dashed rgba(240, 165, 0, 0.4);
    border-radius: 8px;
    max-width: 90%;
  }
  .jk-form { display: flex; gap: 10px; margin-top: 14px; }
  .jk-input {
    flex: 1;
    height: 52px;
    background: #fffdf5;
    border: 1.5px solid #1a1a1a;
    border-radius: 10px;
    color: #1a1a1a;
    padding: 0 16px;
    font-family: 'Georgia', serif;
    font-size: 14pt;
    outline: none;
    transition: box-shadow 200ms, border-color 200ms;
  }
  .jk-input::placeholder { color: #9a8a6a; font-style: italic; }
  .jk-input:focus { border-color: #f0a500; box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(240, 165, 0, 0.18); }
  .jk-btn {
    background: #1a1a1a;
    color: #f0a500;
    border: 1.5px solid #1a1a1a;
    height: 52px;
    padding: 0 22px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 11pt;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 200ms, transform 150ms, box-shadow 200ms;
  }
  .jk-btn:hover:not(:disabled) { background: #2a2a2a; transform: translateY(-1px); }
  .jk-btn:disabled { opacity: 0.55; cursor: wait; }
  .jk-status {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 9pt;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: lowercase;
    color: rgba(255, 247, 223, 0.55);
  }
  .jk-status-dot { width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; background: #35c46a; box-shadow: 0 0 6px rgba(53, 196, 106, 0.7); }
  .jk-status-sep { opacity: 0.5; }
  #jk-avg, #jk-left { color: rgba(255, 247, 223, 0.45); }
  .jk-clear {
    margin-left: auto;
    background: none;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 247, 223, 0.2);
    border-radius: 6px;
    color: rgba(255, 247, 223, 0.55);
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 8.5pt;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: lowercase;
    padding: 4px 10px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .jk-clear:hover { color: #fff7df; border-color: rgba(255, 247, 223, 0.45); }
  .jk-note { margin-top: 26px; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--muted-hi); max-width: 760px; }
</style>

</Layout>
